  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 357 PM CDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nWith the colder air mass moving south Monday night will see\ncooler, more near normal temperatures on Tuesday with highs only\nin the upper 50s to low 60s across the northern Sandhills and in\nthe 60s to low 70s across the southern Sandhills into southwest\nNebraska. With extra moisture streaming into the region and a\ndisturbance moving in, will see chances for precipitation\nincreasing heading into Tuesday night. The greatest potential\nfor precipitation will be Wednesday, with scattered to\nwidespread rain showers expected. At this time, however\nprecipitation values look to be low, generally a quarter of an\ninch or less. Scattered rain chances will linger into early\nThursday, with cooler temperatures expected through the week.\nThursday night and Friday night still looks to be the coldest\nfor overnight lows and will need to continue to monitor the\nnorthwest Sandhills as the current trend continues to come in\ncooler and may need frost/freeze headlines by the end of the\nweek.",
